      "url": "https://direct.mit.edu/qss/article/2/4/1399/108050/Data-citation-and-the-citation-graph",
      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5286f344725dc8e5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTherefore, the graph should be a timestamped “append-only” structure in a way similar to the distributed ledgers. Thus, it should only be possible to insert data in it without the possibility to overwrite or modify already existing information. Among others, these requirements are necessary for the computation of impact factors (Garfield, 2006) where it is necessary to know the number of citations received by a journal in the past 2 years.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5286f344725dc8e5\">>>",
